Hi Henrik,

Sorry I have one more question to bug you. The urls in the df (by df <- readDataFrame(db);) point to UCSCgenome browser with NCBI36/hg18 assembly. I looked at the http://www.aroma-project.org/chipTypes/GenomeWideSNP_6 page resource part, the SNP6 chip type files are listed as based on hg19 (Human Genome build v36.1). This is a typo, right? I thought it should be hg18. So the Cbs out put is also based on hg18, right?

Thanks a lot for the help!

Sean

On Fri, Aug 2, 2013 at 11:03 AM, Henrik Bengtsson <henrik.b...@aroma-project.org> wrote:
> On Thu, Aug 1, 2013 at 6:37 PM, ying chen <njs...@gmail.com> wrote:
